his, X barely appears in early records, first mentioned in Majha Pravas (1907) by Vishnubhat Godse, where X is just called a Queen's maid.\nWhile Queen was fighting to secure her kingdom for her adopted son, X's motives remain less documented, raising questions about whose sense of patriotism was more selfless.\nQueen stood on the weaker side in the gender division, but in the discourse on caste, she belonged to the strongest. X, on the other hand, was marginalised in both simultaneously.\nToday, X is remembered as a Dalit virangana and a symbol of resistance, especially as a model of Kori womanhood. X also appears in Kangana's Manikarnika, played by Ankita Lokhande.\nID X", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:32:28Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Chinnamma?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:32:34Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Jhalkari", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:32:35Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "lakshmi bai", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:32:40Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "person who covered for her", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:33:43Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "great question and crack", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T14:33:59Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "correct answer: Jhalkaribai ‎<attached: 00117392-PHOTO-2026-04-15-07-33-59.jpg>", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]